<!--
  Foreground layer of the adaptive icon. **Viewport 108, the whole drawing inside the central
  66 dp circle.**

  The 18 dp of margin on each edge are not fussiness: the mask belongs to the manufacturer, not
  to us — circle, squircle, teardrop, strictly a circle on Wear OS — and the launcher applies a
  parallax offset on top of that. Anything leaving the 66 dp circle can disappear on a device we
  have not tested. The check fits on one line: the distance from every point to the centre
  (54, 54) must stay under 33.

    pivot  (54, 27)                    distance 27
    bob  centre (69.4, 69.3) radius 9.5  distance 21.7 + 9.5 = 31.2
    arc  bottom (54, 72)               distance 18

  The drawing is a pendulum displaced by 20 degrees, with the arc of its travel. The subject is
  not decorative: the period of a pendulum does not depend on the amplitude of its displacement,
  and that is exactly the product's argument — the rhythm between movements is stable where
  their count is not. The arc carries the amplitude, the rod carries the period.

  No shadow, no gradient, no pre-applied mask: the launcher takes care of that, and an asset that
  ships them ends up with two shadows.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The arc of travel, held back: it is the amplitude, and amplitude is what the product
         sets aside in favour of the period. It has to read, not dominate. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M38.61,69.29 A45,45 0 0 0 69.39,69.29"
        android:strokeAlpha="0.55"
        android:strokeColor="#6FB2FF"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="3" />

    <!-- The rod. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M54,27 L69.39,69.29"
        android:strokeColor="#6FB2FF"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="5" />

    <!-- The pivot. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#6FB2FF"
        android:pathData="M54,27 m-4.5,0 a4.5,4.5 0 1,0 9,0 a4.5,4.5 0 1,0 -9,0" />

    <!-- The bob. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#6FB2FF"
        android:pathData="M69.39,69.29 m-9.5,0 a9.5,9.5 0 1,0 19,0 a9.5,9.5 0 1,0 -19,0" />

</vector>
